-- title:
--   Full-level Weierstrass moduli package, integral over A[j₀]
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes and $M'$ a nonzero natural number, with $\ell \ge 3$ and with $\ell$, $M'$, $2$ and $3$ units in $A$. Assume two equivariance hypotheses: for every $A$-algebra $T$, a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, a variable change $C$ and a quadruple $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ in $T$, if $D$ is a level-$\ell$ structure on $W$ (both points satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation, both $x$-coordinates are roots of $\mathrm{preΨ}_\ell$, and the two independence elements $\mathrm{indepElt}$ are units) then the transformed quadruple is a level-$\ell$ structure on $C \bullet W$; and likewise `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (the two-torsion kernel condition when $p^k=2$, the cyclic generating kernel condition otherwise) is preserved under $W \mapsto C \bullet W$, $h \mapsto$ `kernelVariableChangeDeg`. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, assumed chord–tangent (for each such curve there is an evaluation equivalence to the affine point group that is additive and Galois-equivariant) and origin-normalised (the identity section is an origin-chart section killing $x/y$ and $z/y$), and let $\mathcal{T}$ be a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`: its variable-change and coefficient-change operations move the two sections of a raw Drinfeld pair compatibly with every graded homomorphism of projective model rings realising the variable change, respectively the coefficient map. Assume further that such graded homomorphisms exist, with the irrelevant ideal of the target contained in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source, for every variable change (`hVC`) and every $A$-algebra map (`hCO`). Then the level moduli datum attached to the rigid Weierstrass datum `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯` — curves with unit discriminant carrying a tuple of $\Gamma_0$-type kernel polynomials, one for each prime divisor $p$ of $M'$ at exponent $v_p(M')$, a level-$\ell$ quadruple and a raw Drinfeld pair forming a basis of level $q$, taken up to variable change, with the $j$-invariant as structure map — admits an abstract moduli package $P_0$: an $A$-algebra $B_0$ with a point over $B_0$ through which every point over every $A$-algebra factors uniquely, such that $B_0$ is of finite type over $A$ and integral over the subalgebra $A[j_0]$ generated by the $j$-invariant of the universal point.
--
--   This is the representability statement for the full-level Weierstrass moduli problem — $\Gamma_0$-type kernel data at the level $M'$, a Katz level-$\ell$ structure and a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ — together with finiteness of the representing ring over the $j$-line, in the style of Katz–Mazur's treatment of rigid, relatively representable moduli problems. It is the entry point for the later construction of level structures, completions at points of the $j$-line and the analysis of automorphisms of the moduli problem.
